         <div type="bio">
            <p>As secretary of the New York Society for the Suppression of Vice, John S. Sumner lodged a complaint against <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">The Little Review</name>, in which Ulysses was serialised. The editors <name type="person" key="ande86">Margaret Anderson</name> and <name type="person" key="heap83">Jane Heap</name> were charged with obscenity for publishing the “Nausicaa” episode in their journal’s April 1920 issue, convicted in a New York court, and fined. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
